# What the M28 demo must show, in order: the riscv64 image boots to IEx on
# qemu-system-riscv64's virt machine, the box reports its architecture and the
# interpreter, a module defined at the prompt survives a power cycle, and it
# powers off.
elixos-shim: pid 1, version
iex(1)> IEx.configure(colors: [enabled: false])
=== ELIXOS / RISC-V (riscv64) ===
iex(3)> :erlang.system_info(:system_architecture)
~c"riscv64-unknown-linux-musl"
iex(4)> :erlang.system_info(:emu_flavor)
:emu
iex(5)> (defmodule Demo.Risc do
:riscv_ok
iex(6)> Elixos.save()
{:ok,
elixos-shim: shutdown poweroff
iex(1)> IEx.configure(colors: [enabled: false])
=== ELIXOS / RISC-V (riscv64) ===
iex(3)> Demo.Risc.value()
:riscv_ok
elixos-shim: shutdown poweroff
